<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;LADY RAVENWOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lady Ravenwood is a character who has been hired to bring Felix Flynn in and is part of a larger adventure and intrigue involving a group of thieves and scoundrels."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FELIX FLYNN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Felix Flynn is the infamous thief and scoundrel known for his daring heists and charming demeanor, with a reputation as the greatest thief in the land."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TAVERN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Tavern is a dimly lit establishment where the story begins, filled with various patrons including thieves and scoundrels."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCOUNDRELS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scoundrels refer to a group of thieves and adventurers, including Lady Ravenwood, Felix Flynn, and others, united by a shared quest for fortune and glory."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREASURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Treasure is a valuable item hidden deep within the city's sewers, sought after by the scoundrels and adventurers."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERFECT SCOUNDRELS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Perfect Scoundrels is a drama television series known for its serialized storytelling approach and carefully crafted atmosphere and mood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Perfect Scoundrels is a drama television series that explores the complexities of human relationships, morality, and the gray areas in between, featuring a group of charismatic con artists."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRAMA TELEVISION SERIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Drama Television Series is a genre characterized by character-driven narratives, emotional resonance, and a focus on the complexities of human relationships and morality."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CON ARTISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Con Artists are the main characters in 'Perfect Scoundrels', each with their own distinct backstory and motivations, entangled in a web of deceit and loyalty."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOODED FIGURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Hooded Figure is a mysterious character who sips a mug and watches the interactions in the tavern."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BURLY MAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Burly Man is a character with a thick beard and a menacing scar, known for his loud laughter and interactions with the agile woman."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGILE WOMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Agile Woman is a lithe, agile-looking character with a mischievous glint in her eye, interacting with the burly man."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUARDSMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Guardsmen are a group of soldiers or law enforcement officers that Felix Flynn is charming with tales of his heists."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CITY'S SEWERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The City's Sewers are the location where the Treasure is hidden, a place of mystery and danger."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TELEVISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Television is the medium through which the drama series 'Perfect Scoundrels' is broadcasted."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIMLY LIT ESTABLISHMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Dimly Lit Establishment is another term for the Tavern where the story begins."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHARISMATIC CON ARTISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Charismatic Con Artists are the main characters in 'Perfect Scoundrels', each with their own distinct backstory and motivations."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRAUMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trauma is a theme explored in 'Perfect Scoundrels', affecting the characters' actions and decisions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FORGIVENESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Forgiveness is a theme explored in 'Perfect Scoundrels', impacting the characters' journeys and relationships."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RIGHT AND WRONG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Gray Areas between Right and Wrong are explored in 'Perfect Scoundrels', challenging the characters' moral compasses."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHARACTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Characters in Perfect Scoundrels exhibit moral ambiguity, contributing to the show's depth and complexity."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCORE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The score of Perfect Scoundrels is noted for its effectiveness in heightening tension and emotional impact."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VISUAL AND AUDITORY ELEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Visual and auditory elements are described as hallmarks of drama television, enhancing the narrative atmosphere and mood."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DRAMA TELEVISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Drama television is characterized by its careful crafting of atmosphere and mood, and use of serialized storytelling."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATMOSPHERE AND MOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Atmosphere and mood are carefully crafted in drama television to enhance the narrative."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SERIALIZED STORYTELLING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Serialized storytelling is a technique used in drama television where each episode builds upon the previous one, creating a sense of continuity and urgency."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENSION AND EMOTIONAL IMPACT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tension and emotional impact are heightened through the use of score and visual and auditory elements in drama television."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0156</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;LADY RAVENWOOD&quot;" target="&quot;FELIX FLYNN&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Lady Ravenwood approaches Felix Flynn and becomes part of his game, hinting at a shared quest for fortune and glory."</data>
      <data key="d5">"quest, partnership"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0156</data>
    </edge>
